nd had decided that the Gold Kingdom would offer the most beautiful girl in their kingdom as a bride, to be wed to the most clever man from the Water Kingdom, creating not just a couple but the promise of renewed relations and peace.\n\nWhen it comes time for the rulers to make good on their promise, neither is entirely honest or admirable in their attempts. The Gold Kingdom offers Sara, a kind-hearted, but homely princess while the Water Kingdom marries off Naranbayar, a lanky scholar of modest background. To add insult to injury, the two separately find themselves with a dog (for Sara) and a cat (for Naranbayar) as their partner-to-be. As Sara and Naranbayar individually navigate the palace schemes of their respective homelands, their paths soon converge in a heartwarming new spin on the classic fairytale set-up.\n\n(Source: JAPAN HOUSE Los Angeles)"},"tags":[{"name":"Foreign","rank":80,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Royal Affairs","rank":76,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Primarily Adult Cast","rank":75,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Female Protagonist","rank":75,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Arranged Marriage","rank":74,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Josei","rank":73,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Politics","rank":73,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Male Protagonist","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Heterosexual","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Medieval","rank":70,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Desert","rank":65,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Historical","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Fake Relationship","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Body Image","rank":60,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Swordplay","rank":40,"spoiler":false},{"name":"Fairy Tale","rank":35,"spoiler":false}],"titles":{"display":"Gold Kingdom and Water Kingdom","english":"Gold Kingdom and Water Kingdom","native":"金の国水の国","romaji":"Kin no Kuni Mizu no Kuni","synonyms":[{"language":"ja","source":"bangumi","value":"金の国 水の国"},{"language":"zh","source":"bangumi","value":"金之国 水之国"}]},"trailer":{"id":"ZxYh-ezfyDk","site":"youtube","thumbnail